DECISION: GLOBALLY EFFECTIVE, BUT INJECTED AS AN INDEX, NOT VERBATIM
  global-agents.md is re-injected into every single conversation, so pasting 187 lines of LCEDA detail
  there would tax every unrelated task. Rule 9 therefore carries only what must be true at all times:
    - the trigger condition (any conversation that drives LCEDA)
    - the pointer to the full document and its machine-readable twin
    - four iron rules, chosen because each one prevents silent data loss or a 60-second hang:
        boolean return values lie (importChanges / setNetlist write nothing; getNetlist hangs)
        never experiment on the user's real projects; back up projects before upgrading
        never compute pin/pad coordinates yourself
        clear ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE before any CLI call; PCB writes need 4.1.78+
  Everything else stays in the policy file and is read on demand.

ALSO FIXED: THE POLICY CONTRADICTED ITSELF
  The markdown still announced "deployment status: NOT globally injected", which would have been false the
  moment rule 9 landed. Rewrote that line to say it IS injected, and noted that the global layer holds the
  trigger plus the four rules while the document holds the detail. The JSON "deployment" field was updated
  in lockstep so the two cannot diverge.

